# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the React app (AGENTIC-ARBITER/app)
# Added 2026-08-28 with the React migration. The SOURCE is tracked; these are not.
# `dist/` is the exception worth explaining: the built app is the artefact a judge opens, and the
# README's claim is that it needs no install step. So dist/ is ignored during development and is
# meant to be committed deliberately, once, when the app supersedes demo/index.html.
node_modules/
AGENTIC-ARBITER/app/dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- BUILD INPUTS, MOVED OUT OF THE REPOSITORY 2026-08-28 ----------------------------------------
# 1,039 MB across 2,120 files: imagery, national fields, weather and the live cache. NEVER fetched at
# runtime, proved by reading the page: it fetches only sites.json, unified_sites.json, per-site names
# from that manifest, and api/*, all relative and all inside demo/. So it is a regeneration input, not
# part of what a judge opens.
#
# It now lives at D:\FGHackathon-data with a DIRECTORY JUNCTION at the old path, so all twelve scripts
# that build `os.path.join(IA, "data", ...)` keep working with no code change. Untracked, so it is
# never pushed: tracked bytes fall from 1,823 MB to about 960 MB, inside GitHub's recommended 1 GB.
#
# ⚠ A fresh clone will NOT have it, and cannot regenerate the pipeline without it. That is the
# deliberate trade. CONTEXT/02-ARCHITECTURE.md records what it holds and where it went.
# 🔴 geometry IS NEEDED BY THE SERVER AND IS TRACKED. Measured, not assumed: with data/ absent,
# `live.py selftest` dies on data/geometry/selected_site.json and serve_live.py will not start at all.
# The BROWSER never fetches data/, which is what an earlier note here claimed and it was only half
# true; the SERVER reads geometry at import time. 13 MB, 1,185 files, so it belongs in the repo.
#
# The other four subfolders were each hidden in turn and the selftest still passed, so they are build
# inputs only. They live at D:/FGHackathon-data with a per-folder junction here, which keeps every
# script working and keeps 1,026 MB out of GitHub:
#     imagery 300 MB   weather 229 MB   national_fields 280 MB   live_cache 218 MB
AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/*
!AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/geometry/


# The BUILT app that ships. demo/app/ is tracked on purpose: GitHub Pages can only serve files that
# are committed, and this is the deployable artefact. Its sourcemaps are not committed, which is why
# this is a pattern and not a folder exclusion: 3.6 MB of .map for no reader benefit on a host.
AGENTIC-ARBITER/demo/app/**/*.map

# The per-site intermediates the report build writes beside its fonts. Every one is regenerated from
# demo/*.json on each build and named with a leading underscore for exactly this reason. The three
# instanced Inter faces in the same folder ARE committed: they are the output of
# tools/make_report_fonts.py, and committing them means a host can build the report without fontTools.
AGENTIC-ARBITER/src/reportassets/_*

# The demo voiceover script is a working document for the video, not part of the
# shipped artefact. Kept on the local drive only, at the user's direction.
DEMO-SCRIPT-2m50.md

# The FINISHED VIDEO and the recordings it is cut from, for the same reason and by the same
# instruction. These were untracked but not ignored, which one `git add -A` would have undone:
# the MP4 alone is 58 MB. AGENTIC-ARBITER-demo.mp4 is rebuilt by the session harness from
# DEMO_FINAL.wav plus the spliced clips, so nothing here is a source that cannot be remade
# except the recordings themselves, which are the user's own voice.
AGENTIC-ARBITER-demo.mp4
DEMO_FINAL.wav
live agent.wav
economic.wav
FGfield.wav
